---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { PROFILE } from '../data/profile';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What ORIZ.IN does and does not collect, how local tools work, which optional services exist, and how to exercise your choices."
  lastUpdated="25 October 2026"
>
  <p>
    ORIZ.IN is operated by {PROFILE.name} ({PROFILE.email}). This policy
    explains the limited data involved in visiting the site. It applies to
    <a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url}</a> and its subpages, not to third-party sites
    that we link to.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>There are no accounts, logins, or user profiles on ORIZ.IN.</li>
    <li>
      Interactive tools process their input in your browser. The tool code does
      not send your input to ORIZ.IN.
    </li>
    <li>
      Theme preference and optional learning-path progress are saved in your
      own browser using <code>localStorage</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Analytics and advertising integrations are optional, inactive by default,
      and only load when valid configuration is supplied by the operator.
    </li>
    <li>
      The hosting provider processes ordinary request data to deliver and
      protect the site. Email and social services process data when you choose
      to use them.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data we handle</h2>

  <h3>Tool inputs</h3>
  <p>
    Formatting, conversion, calculation, inspection, and preview features run
    locally in JavaScript or WebAssembly. The site does not transmit the text,
    files, numbers, or diagrams you put into a tool to a server controlled by
    ORIZ.IN. Tool pages display whether processing is local. Do not treat a
    browser tool as a secure vault: your device, browser extensions, and other
    software may have their own access to local data.
  </p>

  <h3>Hosting and request data</h3>
  <p>
    ORIZ.IN is served through Cloudflare Pages. When you request a page,
    Cloudflare may process technical information such as your IP address,
    requested URL, browser headers, timestamps, and security signals in order to
    deliver content, cache it, and protect the service from abuse. Cloudflare
    handles that data under its own privacy terms. ORIZ.IN does not use this
    information to build reader profiles.
  </p>

  <h3>Local preferences</h3>
  <p>
    The site stores a small theme preference under the key
    <code>oriz-theme</code>. If you mark learning-path steps complete, the site
    stores that path’s selections under a key beginning with
    <code>oriz-path:</code>. These values stay in your browser, are not
    transmitted by the application, and can be removed by clearing site data.
  </p>

  <h3>Search</h3>
  <p>
    Search queries are processed in your browser against a static JSON index.
    The query may appear in the page URL and your browsing history. It is not
    sent to ORIZ.IN analytics. The server sees the request for the index file,
    not the words you typed into the search field.
  </p>

  <h3>Email and social contact</h3>
  <p>
    If you email {PROFILE.email}, your email provider and ours process the
    message and its metadata. If you open an issue on GitHub or contact me on a
    social platform, that service processes the content under its own terms.
    GitHub issues are public by design. Do not send secrets or personal data you
    would not want retained by those providers.
  </p>

  <h3>Optional analytics</h3>
  <p>
    Google Analytics 4 and Microsoft Clarity integrations are present in the
    codebase but disabled unless the operator explicitly enables them with
    valid project identifiers. When enabled, they may collect page views,
    device and browser information, approximate location, interaction data, and
    identifiers or cookies controlled by those providers. Tool interfaces are
    marked to be masked from session recording, and no tool input values or
    search queries are intentionally sent as analytics events. Clarity can
    still collect other interaction data outside the masked areas, so enabling
    it is a privacy decision that requires appropriate notice and, where
    required, consent.
  </p>

  <h3>Optional advertising</h3>
  <p>
    Google AdSense is not loaded unless a valid publisher configuration is
    supplied. If advertising is enabled later, Google and its partners may use
    cookies or similar identifiers to select, measure, and limit ads, subject
    to their policies and any consent requirements that apply in your region.
    Ads will be labelled and kept separate from tool controls and editorial
    content.
  </p>

  <h3>Donations</h3>
  <p>
    Donation links open Buy Me a Coffee, a third-party service. ORIZ.IN does not
    receive payment card details. The provider processes the payment and account
    information under its own privacy policy. Donations are voluntary.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
  <p>
    ORIZ.IN’s application does not set its own advertising or analytics cookies.
    It uses browser <code>localStorage</code> for the preferences described
    above. Cloudflare may set security or performance-related cookies as the
    hosting provider. Optional third-party analytics or ads would introduce
    their own cookies or identifiers only if the operator enables those
    services. See the <a href="/cookies/">cookies and analytics page</a> for the
    current status and controls.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we process data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>To provide the site</strong> and respond to requests, including
      ordinary hosting, caching, and security processing.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To answer you</strong> when you send an email or a correction.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>With consent, where required</strong>, for optional analytics or
      advertising that the operator enables.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To protect rights and safety</strong>, including investigating
      abuse, fraud, or security incidents.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Browser preferences remain until you clear them. Emails remain in the mail
    system for as long as needed to answer the request and keep a reasonable
    record of corrections or legal obligations. Hosting, analytics, advertising,
    and social providers retain data according to their own policies. ORIZ.IN
    does not maintain a separate visitor database.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can clear local preferences through your browser’s site-data settings,
    use browser privacy controls, and choose not to interact with third-party
    services. If you have sent personal information by email, you can ask for
    access, correction, or deletion by writing to
    <a href={`mailto:${PROFILE.email}`}>{PROFILE.email}</a>. Depending on where
    you live, you may have additional rights under applicable data-protection
    law. We will respond within a reasonable period and may ask you to verify
    that you are the person who sent the original request.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    ORIZ.IN is a general technical reference intended for adults and is not
    directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal
    information from children. If you believe a child has sent personal
    information, contact us so we can address it.
  </p>

  <h2>International processing</h2>
  <p>
    Cloudflare and other service providers may process data in countries other
    than yours. They are responsible for their own transfer mechanisms and
    safeguards. ORIZ.IN does not deliberately route reader data to additional
    processors beyond the services described in this policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    The site may link to or optionally load the following providers. Their
    privacy policies and settings control their processing:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare</a> (hosting and security)</li>
    <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google</a> (optional Analytics or AdSense)</li>
    <li><a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft</a> (optional Clarity)</li>
    <li><a href="https://www.buymeacoffee.com/privacy-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Buy Me a Coffee</a> (voluntary donations)</li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/site/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a> (code hosting and issue tracker)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    The site is delivered over HTTPS, has no login system, and keeps its
    optional data collection minimal. No internet service can promise perfect
    security. Use the tools with ordinary care, and never paste production
    secrets into a web page simply because it processes locally.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    This policy may change as the site adds features or optional services. The
    “last updated” date on this page is the authoritative date. Material changes
    will be reflected here; continued use after a change means the new policy
    applies to future visits.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions or requests about privacy:
    <a href={`mailto:${PROFILE.email}?subject=Privacy%20question`}>{PROFILE.email}</a>.
    See also the <a href="/cookies/">cookies page</a> and
    <a href="/terms/">terms of use</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
